WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.540
Andy: I tried to sit back as far as I could
so there’d be a long awkward silence.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:14.280
Thank you to Dr. Arnn, the platform party,
family and friends.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.440
To the class of 2015, congratulations.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.850
We made it.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.970
Before I begin my speech, I find it appropriate
to brag on behalf of this class to all of

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:36.900
you here, the class of 2015 is the smartest
class ever admitted to Hillsdale College.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.090
As of last night, it is also the most philanthropic.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.580
Last summer the other class officers and I
set a goal for 50% class participation in

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.560
our give-back campaign.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:57.410
According to my count, we have reached our
goal.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:02.600
Once we have finalized these pledges, several
generous alumni will help us establish a scholarship

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:08.859
for next year’s incoming freshman as a token
of our love for this place.

00:01:08.859 --> 00:01:15.680
One more note … Two years ago at RA training,
Dr. Arnn made a deal with Matt O’Sullivan

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.060
that if he kept his 4-point, Dr. Arnn would
buy him any book up to a certain amount.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.940
As Matt is too humble to say this for himself,
I feel obligated to remind the good doctor

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.460
of this.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:35.509
Male: He doesn’t remember.

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:40.640
Dr. Arnn: I have to interrupt you.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.460
Matthew, what was the amount?

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.830
$100?

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:50.460
I’m losing money like crazy.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.780
Send me an email and remind me, and I’ll
send you the book, or the $100.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.490
I made a bet with Jack Babbott.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.540
He’s going to watch this tape.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.950
He gave a big gift for the chapel, and with
the architect sitting there, and with Rich

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.410
Paway sitting there, he said, “You’ll
never build this chapel for this amount.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.060
It’s going to cost four times as much.”

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:20.360
I said, in a rash moment, “I bet you $5,000
to your favorite charity against $5,000 to

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.880
mine that we can build it for that.”

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:29.261
I looked at Rich and I looked at the architect,
and they both nodded their heads, and I’m

00:02:29.261 --> 00:02:33.010
getting ready to write a check to Jack Babbott
for $5,000.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:38.040
Now it’s $5,100.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:46.420
Andy: Thank you, Dr. Arnn.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:59.760
When I began to write this speech last night
… I’m really glad you all thought that

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.370
was a joke.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.620
I considered several different approaches.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.800
After all, what is one supposed to talk about
in a commencement speech?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.180
Should I reflect on the last 4 years here?

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.460
Reminiscing about the highlights of my experience,
and attempt to generalize them so that everyone

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.500
might identify.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.300
Not to say that there’s anything wrong or
at all inaccurate about remembering those

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.560
nights when the cell phones go silent, the
lap tops are shut tight, and the conversation

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.320
amongst friends soars far and wide.

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.720
After all, it is true that most of us, if
not all of us, have had those experiences.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.130
That is a good thing.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.150
This is a commencement address.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.121
For a while now, I have found it odd that
we called the graduation of seniors in the

00:03:41.121 --> 00:03:42.320
spring commencement.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.120
Dr. Ward pointed this out.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.930
Commencement refers to a beginning.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.380
To make a start or enter in upon something.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:54.180
Yet, we are concluding our education here,
and our time has come to an end.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.770
Of course many of you probably want to respond
with, “But our education never ends.”

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.380
To which I would respond, “You’re right.”

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.510
Now shut up, I’m giving the speech.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.870
Why did we name the ceremony marking our departure
from this school, this place and these people,

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.770
in terms of a beginning?

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.760
I had a theory.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.810
Commencement is an attempt to give this moment
a particular significance.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:21.900
In a conscience manner, we want this moment
of transition to be one of hope and of promise,

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.639
a setting out from home and confidence enjoyed
towards some glorious fate.

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:29.939
This day is the first day of the rest of our
lives, and 4 years here have prepared us to

00:04:29.939 --> 00:04:33.180
meet it with bright eyes and full hearts.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.550
If only that were true.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.639
In order to make us even more self-conscious
about what is happening right here, right

00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:41.060
now, I’ll tell you how I’m actually feeling.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.780
I am terrified.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:48.759
The last time that I was this terrified was
1,350 days ago.

00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:52.210
August 28th, 2011, in our freshman convocation.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:57.240
I’ll be honest with you, like many here
today, I had not wanted to come to Hillsdale.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.729
In fact, it was my last choice.

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:02.849
Some of you, including my family, knew that.

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:05.409
Until now, I have never told anyone the real
reason why.

00:05:05.409 --> 00:05:10.090
It wasn’t because of pride or stubbornness,
or some other pretended thing.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:14.180
I didn’t come to this school because I was
terrified.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:20.050
Terrified to fail, terrified to succeed, terrified
of the unknown.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.210
This college is hard.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.260
What we do here is difficult from beginning
to end without exception.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:28.740
The worst part is that it is completely up
to us to do it.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.060
Sure we have the support of so many wonderful
people, but the fundamental responsibility

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.349
lies with us.

00:05:35.349 --> 00:05:39.900
The words of Albert Camus, from Dr. Jackson’s
Great Books class come to mind.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.690
I didn’t know that freedom is not a reward
or a decoration that is celebrated with champagne,

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.770
nor yet a gift, a box of dainties to make
you lick your chops.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:52.060
No, it’s a chore on the contrary, and a
long distance race.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.180
Quite solitary and very exhausting.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:59.370
At the end of all, freedom is a court sentence.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:04.199
That’s why freedom is too heavy to bear,
especially when you’re down with a fever

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:07.470
or are distressed, or love nobody.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:12.969
1,350 days ago we stood together at East Lawn
and at the prompting of Dr. Arnn, we faced

00:06:12.969 --> 00:06:16.999
our parents and loved ones, hugged them and
walked up to that hill to find those mentor

00:06:16.999 --> 00:06:21.750
groups we now laughingly remember, and we
begin our journey.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:26.610
Today, 1,350 days later, we find ourselves
together again.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.949
Today, I’m still terrified.

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:37.180
Terrified to fail, terrified to succeed, terrified
of the unknown.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:42.099
Terrified because I’m about to leave the
best friends for which a man could ever hope.

00:06:42.099 --> 00:06:46.229
Last year Josh Andrew asked on this occasion,
“Was it worth it?”

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:51.759
This year I ask the question, “Is that … Whatever
we are leaving this for, worth it?”

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:56.039
My answer is simple, “Yes and no.”

00:06:56.039 --> 00:06:59.699
No because a few of us … Just a few of us,
will ever have another chance to study these

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:04.319
great things, to spend our days in leisure
and contemplation, and enjoy the immediate

00:07:04.319 --> 00:07:08.030
presence of friends engaged in the same activity
of soul.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.169
Not to mention that if we were to continue
all of the stupid things we’ve done here,

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:17.490
most of us would live in boxes without a prospect
of a real job.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:22.970
I say, “Yes,” that whatever is out there
is worth leaving this for, because we were

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.449
never meant to stay here.

00:07:25.449 --> 00:07:29.410
The hard truth of this college is that we
live and learn here for a short time, during

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:33.080
which we are formed and molded to live in
the world.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.870
We are called from here to love and to teach
others, to show them the beauty that we have

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:41.680
been shown, to suffer and struggle, and do
the difficult activity of living.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.139
Often it will be thankless.

00:07:43.139 --> 00:07:46.479
Often, it will be suffering.

00:07:46.479 --> 00:07:49.889
Always though, it should be joyous.

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:53.099
We are called and we must respond.

00:07:53.099 --> 00:07:56.479
The funny thing about what we were doing here
today is that no matter how hard we try, no

00:07:56.479 --> 00:08:00.889
matter how flowing our robes are, or how many
pictures we take, we cannot give this day

00:08:00.889 --> 00:08:02.379
meaning.

00:08:02.379 --> 00:08:07.050
That isn’t to say that today isn’t significant,
because in a very real way, this is the most

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.740
significant day of our lives.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:12.740
For the first time in 4 years, we are gathered
together in one place.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:18.139
We have all grown and flourished in a variety
of astounding ways.

00:08:18.139 --> 00:08:21.470
This moment is not significant because of
the robes or the pictures, or because we want

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:22.719
it to be.

00:08:22.719 --> 00:08:27.210
The significance and overwhelming meaning
of this moment right here right now is not

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:31.439
the result of our conscious choice to make
it so, but comes from all our experiences

00:08:31.439 --> 00:08:32.439
until now.

00:08:32.439 --> 00:08:40.219
Now we stand at the end of this journey, staring
into what may seem to be an abyss.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.979
This abyss should not terrify us but give
us hope.

00:08:42.979 --> 00:08:49.040
Because in its darkness is not futility and
nothingness, but endless possibility for greatness.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.230
The unknown is just that, unknown.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:57.940
We can only choose how we greet it, with fear
and trembling, or with wonder.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.140
I return to the words of Camu.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.830
“At the end of all freedom is a court sentence.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.880
That’s why freedom is too heavy to bear,
especially when you’re down with a fever,

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.209
or are distressed, or love nobody.”

00:09:11.209 --> 00:09:14.459
I think that this is right, because after
4 years here, we have found freedom to be

00:09:14.459 --> 00:09:15.459
a chore.

00:09:15.459 --> 00:09:19.300
It has been a long distance race, at times
quite solitary and very exhausting, and far

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.329
too heavy to bear.

00:09:21.329 --> 00:09:25.190
This is the fate to which we have dedicated
ourselves, and our commitment to this college

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.279
and to each other.

00:09:28.279 --> 00:09:31.720
Here at the end of it all, this realization
is the moment to which our education has led

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:32.720
us.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.860
To recognize the difficulty of what we have
chosen to do, and not merely to face it, but

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.320
to thrive in the face of it.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.769
We have not simply overcome suffering.

00:09:42.769 --> 00:09:48.560
We have been formed by it for a future far
more glorious than any we can conceive.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:53.509
We need only look back at those men and women
who helped raise us, our parents, for a model

00:09:53.509 --> 00:09:55.660
of this.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.949
Consider what it means to bear a child.

00:09:57.949 --> 00:09:59.470
Bringing into this world new life.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:04.480
A helpless and vulnerable person for whom
you are wholly responsible.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:09.600
This burden is terrifying, but they are here
today, not because of fear for responsibility,

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:14.130
but out of love for the life that they have
helped form, and in the process been formed

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.730
by.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.180
They recognize the beautify of this moment.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:22.160
Not because it isn’t a moment without strife
and despair, but they recognize the beautify

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.230
of this moment, because they have persevered
through those things.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:32.101
They have learned to love that which is true
and good.

00:10:32.101 --> 00:10:35.149
From this moment forward, we will share in
this beauty, and not because it isn’t suffering

00:10:35.149 --> 00:10:39.589
or pain or struggle, but because through those
things, our hearts and souls have been formed

00:10:39.589 --> 00:10:43.200
to a greater love of that which is good and
beautiful.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.690
After all, one sees clearly only with the
heart.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:51.810
Anything essential is invisible to the eyes.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.630
Today I thank God and I thank all of you,
because we know that this freedom we undertake

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.370
is not too heavy.

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:59.949
We love just as we are loved.

00:10:59.949 --> 00:11:05.399
We have the people around us today, our family,
our friends, and each other, to thank for

00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:07.639
that.

00:11:07.639 --> 00:11:14.180
As we gather here together again, I have faith
this love will abide.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:17.540
Through it, we will know beauty.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.529
Through it, we have a hope that leads us beyond
the confines of this world.

